---
import { contactFormDetails } from '../../consts';
import CustomButton from '../CustomButton.astro';
import Input from '../HTML/Input.astro';
---

{/* novalidate: with type="email" the browser blocks the submit itself and
    shows its own grey bubble, so our own message — the one that says
    "Did you mean @gmail.com?" — never got the chance to appear. One
    voice, ours, on every field. */}
<form id="contact-form" class="space-y-8" novalidate>
	{/* The box no human can see. A browser skips it because it is off the
	    page and out of the tab order; a bot fills in everything it finds.
	    Anything in here means the submission is automated, and it is
	    dropped without a word so whatever is doing it learns nothing. */}
	<p class="cf-pot" aria-hidden="true">
		<label>
			Leave this empty
			<input type="text" name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
		</label>
	</p>
	{
		contactFormDetails.map((ele) => (
			<Input textWhite {...ele} id={ele.name} errorID={`${ele.name}-error`} />
		))
	}
	<CustomButton id="form-button" type="submit" class="w-fit block ml-auto rounded-full !px-16">
		Submit
	</CustomButton>
</form>

<style>
	.cf-pot {
		position: absolute;
		left: -9999px;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.msg {
		border: 1px solid red;
		padding: 12px 24px;
		border-radius: 12px;
	}
</style>

{/* ── the handler is not in this file any more ──────────────────────
    It used to be, as a long component script below this markup, and
    that is exactly why the form was dead in production.

    (That sentence used to spell the tag out literally. Don't. Vite's
    dependency scanner looks for the opening tag with a plain text
    search and does not know this is a comment, so it took the rest of
    the prose for JavaScript and brought the whole dev server down with
    "Expected ';' but found 'this'".)

    A component script is bundled per page and runs once, when that page
    is first parsed. This site navigates with swup: the URL changes and
    the markup is swapped, but the document is never reloaded, so no page
    script runs a second time. The form therefore worked if you typed
    /contact into the address bar, and did nothing whatsoever if you
    clicked "Contact" in the nav — which is how nearly everyone arrives.
    The button simply had no listener on it.

    The newsletter had the same bug and was fixed the same way. The logic
    now lives in src/scripts/contactForm.ts and is called from the init
    list in MainLayout, which runs on first load and on every swup
    contentReplaced. That list is the only place on this site where a
    handler can be attached and be relied upon to stay attached.

    The call below is a belt-and-braces for a direct page load, so the
    form is live even before the layout's list has got to it.
    initContactForm marks every form it binds, so the two cannot end up
    double-binding one and sending the brief twice.
    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
<script>
	import { initContactForm } from '../../scripts/contactForm';
	initContactForm();
</script>
